            "review_title": "Review at Mien Luon Thanh Thao",
            "review_text": "LamN\nSingapore, Singapore4905 contributions\n0\nHidden gem for northern Vietnamese noodle soups\nApr 2019 • Couples\nHard to find hole-in-the-wall in an alley-behind-an-alley near the Bến Thành market. However, it’s a clean shop, serving delicately-tasting but delicious northern Vietnamese soups: the specialty is miến lươn (glass noodle soup with eels - deep fried or steamed). They also have yummy chicken phở; to go with that, you should order a plate of boiled chicken liver, heart and gizzard; sometimes they also have baby eggs. Another hard-to-find northern specialty is bún thang - rice vermicelli soup with sausage (giò), chicken, minced pork and sliced omelette. The place opens for breakfast and closes by 1pm, or whenever they run out of food. Extremely popular with an exclusively-local clientèle. The queue in the morning is proof that it’s worth it. The food is quite fine, so non/familiar westerners may find it too bland.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 9, 2019",
